WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.047 --> 00:00:02.240
- Now the best way to
understand the metaverse

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:03.725
is to experience it yourself.

00:00:03.725 --> 00:00:05.611
(alarm beeping)

00:00:05.611 --> 00:00:08.194
(upbeat music)

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:22.060
- I definitely don't
feel very well right now.

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:23.550
And you wouldn't feel well either

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:25.920
if you attempted to spend 24 hours living

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:28.823
in virtual reality or the metaverse.

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:32.070
Don't know what the metaverse is?

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:35.190
That's okay, I'm not
sure anyone really does.

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:37.120
But Meta, formally known as Facebook,

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:39.080
Microsoft and more are defining it

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:41.290
as the virtual world
that is the next phase

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:42.320
of the internet.

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:44.140
In this world, we have digital versions

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:46.740
of ourselves or avatars.

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:48.610
- And we call this the metaverse.

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:50.780
And you're gonna be able
to do almost anything

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:51.860
you can imagine.

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:54.540
Get together with
friends and family, work,

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:56.340
learn, play, shop.

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:58.200
- So I decided why wait?

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.800
And stupidly I dared myself
to visit the metaverse

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:04.840
for a full 24 hours in its
current not-so-great state.

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:06.730
In fact, Meta and others will tell you

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:09.610
that the metaverse isn't even here yet.

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:11.630
But the best way to see the start of it

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:13.380
is through virtual reality.

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:15.310
And since I didn't
wanna pop into a headset

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:17.040
with my kids running around,

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:19.890
I packed my bags and moved
to the Holiday Inn Express

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:21.140
around the corner.

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:22.380
I set a few rules.

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:25.513
The headset can come off to
eat and go to the bathroom.

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:28.530
Yes, I attempted to sleep with it on.

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:30.810
I checked my phone only if it was urgent.

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:33.690
I had notifications
coming into the headset.

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:34.920
It's about to be 6 PM,

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:36.890
which is the start of
my metaverse journey.

00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:39.470
I've got two headsets in
case of technical issues.

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:41.810
And lots of apps and
other things preloaded

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:44.280
for different parts of the day and night.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:45.730
What could go wrong?

00:01:45.730 --> 00:01:47.290
- [Narrator] Welcome to Beat Saber.

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:49.890
Now, cut the cubes in the arrow direction

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:51.053
and match the color.

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:53.510
That was too soon.

00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:55.740
Wait for the beat, wrong direction.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:56.920
Wrong direction.

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:57.980
- She's very mean.

00:01:57.980 --> 00:02:00.070
I started with games like Beat Saber

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:03.070
since right now they're
the most popular use of VR.

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:05.520
And while many games allow
you to play with others,

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:08.420
I had no real friends to play
Beat Saber with that evening.

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:10.070
So I decided to go elsewhere

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:11.990
for some social interaction.

00:02:11.990 --> 00:02:14.690
AltspaceVR, an app that
allows you to hang out

00:02:14.690 --> 00:02:17.280
with other avatars in virtual venues.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:19.650
Okay, I'm gonna customize my avatar

00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:21.380
for a night out.

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:25.470
I guess in the metaverse
I could have short hair.

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:28.690
I wasn't exactly prepared
for what would happen next.

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:31.277
I guess I'll go to this campfire hub.

00:02:31.277 --> 00:02:32.110
Hello?

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:33.710
As soon as I was in the public area,

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:36.690
I started hearing people
talk and chat and.

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:39.170
(woman coughing)

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:41.640
Apparently there are no
masks in the metaverse.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:42.940
I was dropped into an area

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:46.000
with lots of trippy little
LEGO-looking people,

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.220
and I attempted to interview them.

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:50.320
- [Woman] Oh, a journalist are you?

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:53.100
- I wanna learn what you guys do in here.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:54.846
- [Man] Pretty much
everything that you would do

00:02:54.846 --> 00:02:56.010
in the real world.

00:02:56.010 --> 00:02:57.860
- I knew I had really made friends forever

00:02:57.860 --> 00:02:59.800
when they asked me to go to a comedy club

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:02.140
by clicking on this portal thing.

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:04.230
The club was so obviously fake

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:06.040
but my presence in it and the presence

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:08.940
of all these other
people felt really real.

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:10.260
Do you guys have wine?

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:12.570
- Yeah, of course, wine,
everything you want.

00:03:12.570 --> 00:03:14.800
- I even felt awkward when the comedian

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:16.030
hit on my avatar.

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:17.520
- You were the girl I was
trying to find out your name

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:20.630
but I can't 'cause I'm
trying to be subtle.

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:22.420
- I spent a good amount
of time in Altspace

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:25.900
and came away thinking it's
like an AOL chatroom evolved,

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:28.403
which I'm not sure is
a good or a bad thing.

00:03:29.524 --> 00:03:30.817
I need to relax for a moment.

00:03:30.817 --> 00:03:33.484
(clock ticking)

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:36.153
The meditation app is launched.

00:03:39.370 --> 00:03:40.990
Okay.

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:43.330
- [Narrator] Kindness starts with you.

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:44.950
I highly recommend meditation apps

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:47.620
like Guided Meditation or Trip.

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:50.010
It's oddly relaxing and peaceful.

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:51.740
And I could lie to you
and tell you I slept

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:53.110
with the headset on the whole night

00:03:53.110 --> 00:03:54.955
but we have this proof.

00:03:54.955 --> 00:03:57.622
(playful music)

00:03:59.032 --> 00:04:00.290
(alarm beeping)

00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:01.830
I woke up feeling refreshed.

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:05.062
I pulled up some morning
reading in my web browser.

00:04:05.062 --> 00:04:06.490
Got Google News over here,

00:04:06.490 --> 00:04:09.190
The Wall Street Journal website over here.

00:04:09.190 --> 00:04:11.900
And Instagram over here on the right.

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:14.080
And had breakfast at
the foot of Machu Picchu

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:16.310
with a llama in the
National Geographic app.

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:19.200
It's funny, this animal
has legs in the metaverse.

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:21.500
Why do animals get four
legs in the metaverse

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:23.100
and we get zero?

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:26.003
And then I had a pretty
fun and intense workout.

00:04:27.527 --> 00:04:28.800
- Welcome to Supernatural.

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:30.880
Be ready for your first Flow workout.

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:31.950
- There are various types

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:33.800
of workouts you can do in Supernatural,

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:35.610
which involve everything from doing lunges

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:37.933
to using controllers to hit targets.

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:41.200
Working out in the metaverse is great.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:42.470
I got so into it,

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:44.423
I actually lost track of time.

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:48.010
I have a meeting in Spatial in one minute.

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:50.180
I need to change, crap.

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:53.230
Yes, meeting in the metaverse are a thing.

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:54.260
Hi, Erin, I'm Joanna.

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:55.093
Nice to meet you.

00:04:55.093 --> 00:04:56.510
- Hi, thanks for coming.

00:04:56.510 --> 00:04:58.220
- The idea is that instead of Zoom,

00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:00.010
you chat as avatars.

00:05:00.010 --> 00:05:02.230
My first meeting was in
an app called Spatial.

00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:05.100
And, of course, it required
a different avatar.

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:08.870
Yes, that's my actual
face on a floating torso.

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:10.620
I met up with the co-founder of Spatial,

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:13.290
Anand Agarawala, in an NFT art gallery

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:16.740
with works from Ken Kelleher,
AKA Anchorball on display.

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:18.020
And this is a great stop

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:21.740
because it turns out I'm
in an NFT art gallery,

00:05:21.740 --> 00:05:23.993
which sounds like the metaverse to me.

00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:27.840
- Heck yeah, I mean, you
can't get more metaverse-y

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:32.690
than a pixelated dog or
these crazy heads and stuff

00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:34.200
or these beautiful sculptures.

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:35.640
- We also went to a campfire

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:38.220
where I asked him about the lack of legs.

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:40.020
- The headset tracks
your head and your hands

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:42.000
and so we can make it do realistic stuff.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:42.990
What are my legs supposed to do?

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:45.630
We can't actually detect
the signal from your legs.

00:05:45.630 --> 00:05:47.370
Legs are coming, coming soon.

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:49.050
- I quickly had to jump from that meeting

00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:51.150
to another meeting as another avatar

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:53.000
in Horizon Workrooms,

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:56.150
an app made by Meta,
formerly known as Facebook.

00:05:56.150 --> 00:05:58.330
Oh I see, so it's kind of like
you've gotta really put it

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:00.400
on the board.

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:02.700
You can even invite
people from the real verse

00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:04.940
who happen to be on their webcams.

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:06.880
But again, there was this real feeling

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:08.290
of presence in the room.

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:10.210
I felt like I was actually sitting across

00:06:10.210 --> 00:06:12.290
from my editor, Wilson, in this meeting.

00:06:12.290 --> 00:06:13.830
- It's like in Ghostbusters,

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:15.940
I'm a full-torso apparition.

00:06:15.940 --> 00:06:17.463
You don't need legs.

00:06:18.490 --> 00:06:20.840
Oh no, Joanna's looking under the table.

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:22.440
That's so scary.

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:24.670
- Yes, meeting metaverse is fun

00:06:24.670 --> 00:06:27.650
if you don't do it for four hours on end.

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:30.040
That was so much time in avatar meetings.

00:06:30.040 --> 00:06:32.283
My eyes hurt and my head hurts.

00:06:33.260 --> 00:06:35.200
So what did I learn from this adventure

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:37.620
other than I'd never
recommend you do this?

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:39.200
Well, a few things.

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:40.710
It's clear why big tech companies

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:41.930
are fighting over this.

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:42.840
There's an opportunity

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:45.270
to build the underlying platform here.

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:48.200
One avatar with legs living across games,

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:50.413
workout apps, meetings and more.

00:06:50.413 --> 00:06:52.980
Meta's Meaghan Fitzgerald told me as much.

00:06:52.980 --> 00:06:55.490
- And the metaverse is not
gonna be built by one company.

00:06:55.490 --> 00:06:58.110
That there are other
companies, organizations,

00:06:58.110 --> 00:07:02.280
creators that maybe will use our avatars

00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:04.510
and allow people to move
from one place to another

00:07:04.510 --> 00:07:06.280
while still feeling like themselves.

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:08.750
- Then there's the privacy
tools and moderation.

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:10.650
It's gonna be insane judging

00:07:10.650 --> 00:07:13.120
from my brief comedy club experience.

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:15.050
And then headsets will need to be smaller

00:07:15.050 --> 00:07:17.910
and more comfortable and
run for longer on a charge.

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:19.900
Thank you guys, my headset's
gonna die in five minutes.

00:07:19.900 --> 00:07:23.150
So yes, it's certainly the
early days of the metaverse.

00:07:23.150 --> 00:07:25.160
But lock yourself in a room like this

00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:27.033
and you can really see the potential.

